---
import AsciiDivider from './AsciiDivider.astro';
---

<div class="about-sections">
    <section aria-labelledby="about-heading">
        <h2 id="about-heading">About me</h2>
        <p>
            Computer Science undergraduate at BINUS University with an interest in cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, and backend development.
            I enjoy building secure and practical systems, especially solutions that combine AI with modern security approaches.
            Constantly exploring new technologies and improving my skills through projects and hands-on experience.
        </p>
    </section>
    <AsciiDivider />
    <section aria-labelledby="now-heading">
        <h2 id="now-heading">What I'm up to</h2>
        <p>
            Currently on an internship at Plaza Toyota as a System Engineer, working on backend and managing Omnichannel integration using Copilot Agent
            service for Plaza customers.
        </p>
    </section>
    <AsciiDivider />
    <section aria-labelledby="portrait-heading">
        <h2 id="portrait-heading">What do I look like</h2>
        <figure class="portrait">
            <img src="/shadowsmoke.jpg" alt="orang ganteng" width="250" height="250" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Pretty much</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </section>
    <AsciiDivider />
    <section aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
        <h2 id="projects-heading">My projects</h2>
        <dl class="projects">
            <dt><a href="https://github.com/bavarianprayoga/currencyforecast" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Currency Forecaster</a></dt>
            <dd>An application that forecasts the directional movement of a currency over the next n days using LightGBM, predicting whether it will trend upward or downward.</dd>
            <dt><a href="https://github.com/bavarianprayoga/landscapecolorizer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Landscape Colorizer</a></dt>
            <dd>A landscape image colorization application that converts black-and-white scenery into color using a hybrid architecture combining ResNet-18, U-Net, and skip connections.</dd>
        </dl>
    </section>
</div>
